  "name": "Curve Discount",
  "description": "On the 2-minute BTC up/down market, trade only the last 30 seconds. A hand-fitted fair-value curve maps the absolute move from window open to the leading side's worth: 0.02% moved is about 55 cents, 0.05% about 65, 0.10% about 80, 0.15% or more about 92. During the last 30 seconds, whenever the leading side trades at least 5 cents below the curve, buy it — once per window. At window rollover, reset and wait for the next window's endgame.",
